%I A398976 #16 Oct 19 2026 18:52:47
%S A398976 1,1,7,27,128,555,2846,14710,81905,472836,2857936
%N A398976 Number of nonisomorphic rectangular g-dimonoids of order n.
%C A398976 A g-dimonoid is an algebraic structure (D,-|,|-) consisting of a set D equipped with two associative binary operations -| and |- satisfying the following axioms:
%C A398976    (x -| y) -| z = x -| (y |- z),
%C A398976    (x -| y) |- z = x |- (y |- z).
%C A398976 A g-dimonoid (D,-|,|-) is called rectangular if both (D,-|) and (D,|-) are rectangular semigroups in the sense that
%C A398976    x -| y -| z = x -| z   and   x |- y |- z = x |- z
%C A398976 for all x,y,z from D.
%H A398976 Volodymyr M. Gavrylkiv, <a href="https://doi.org/10.30970/ms.66.1.24-37">On the number of g-dimonoids of small order</a>, Mat. Stud. 66(1) (2026), 24-37.
%H A398976 Volodymyr M. Gavrylkiv, <a href="https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2607.29641">On the number of g-dimonoids of small order</a>, arXiv:2607.29641 [math.GR] (2026).
%H A398976 Volodymyr M. Gavrylkiv, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1080/00927872.2026.2712633">On dimonoids of small order</a>, Commun. Algebra (2026), 1-15.
%H A398976 Volodymyr M. Gavrylkiv, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23321485">Enumeration and lists of nonisomorphic rectangular g-dimonoids</a>, Zenodo (2026).
%H A398976 Volodymyr M. Gavrylkiv, <a href="https://gist.github.com/vgavrylkiv/9a066fc0c6e0c1283baa231cb85c2895">C++ program for computing all pairwise nonisomorphic rectangular g-dimonoids and dimonoids</a>, GitHub Gist (2026).
%e A398976 For n = 2, there are exactly 7 pairwise nonisomorphic rectangular g-dimonoids (D,-|,|-) on the set D={0,1}. Rows and columns are ordered as 0,1. The Cayley tables of all seven g-dimonoids are listed below.
%e A398976 g-dimonoid #1:
%e A398976    -|:   |-:
%e A398976    0 0   0 0
%e A398976    0 0   0 0
%e A398976 g-dimonoid #2:
%e A398976    -|:   |-:
%e A398976    0 0   1 1
%e A398976    0 0   1 1
%e A398976 g-dimonoid #3:
%e A398976    -|:   |-:
%e A398976    0 0   0 1
%e A398976    0 0   0 1
%e A398976 g-dimonoid #4:
%e A398976    -|:   |-:
%e A398976    0 0   0 0
%e A398976    1 1   0 0
%e A398976 g-dimonoid #5:
%e A398976    -|:   |-:
%e A398976    0 0   0 0
%e A398976    1 1   1 1
%e A398976 g-dimonoid #6:
%e A398976    -|:   |-:
%e A398976    0 0   0 1
%e A398976    1 1   0 1
%e A398976 g-dimonoid #7:
%e A398976    -|:   |-:
%e A398976    0 1   0 1
%e A398976    0 1   0 1
%Y A398976 Cf. A027851, A390162, A400568, A400569, A400570, A400914, A400915.
